# Stock Market Dashboard - Development Note

## Development Approach

I adopted a systematic, full-stack development approach starting with comprehensive project planning using a todo management system. The development followed a mobile-first responsive design methodology, ensuring optimal user experience across all devices. I prioritized building a solid foundation with mock data and API structure before implementing the user interface, allowing for seamless integration between frontend and backend components.

The architecture emphasizes modularity and scalability, with separate components for different dashboard sections (company list, charts, predictions) and a well-structured API layer. I implemented a professional fintech design system with carefully selected colors, typography, and spacing that conveys trust and sophistication.

## Technologies Used

**Frontend:** Next.js 14 with TypeScript for type safety and modern React features, Tailwind CSS for responsive styling, Recharts for interactive data visualization, and shadcn/ui for consistent component design.

**Backend:** Next.js API routes providing RESTful endpoints, with comprehensive error handling and data validation.

**Data Management:** Mock dataset simulating real Indian stock market data (NSE companies) with realistic historical patterns and volatility.

**Deployment:** Docker containerization, Vercel and Railway deployment configurations, with PostgreSQL database schemas for production scaling.

## Challenges Encountered

The primary challenge was creating realistic stock market data that accurately reflects Indian market behavior and volatility patterns. Implementing responsive design for complex financial charts required careful consideration of touch interactions and mobile viewport constraints. Balancing feature richness with performance optimization, especially for the AI prediction algorithms and chart rendering, demanded strategic component optimization. Additionally, ensuring the API design could scale from mock data to real financial data sources required thoughtful abstraction layers.

